lf-cent amounts (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66 instead of 2.67).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 748729, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S3QR9AvLjFFs6W8ZHhmBuG", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 748729, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S3QR9AvLjFFs6W8ZHhmBuG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 754952, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. The test expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`, so it failed.\n- **Fix:** I made a one-line change on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` so `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the new head (`0a9452f727`). That run also passed.\n- **Behaviour change:** Amounts that land exactly on a half cent now round to the nearest even cent instead of always up (e.g. `2.665` \u2192 `2.66`, not `2.67`). I noted this in the PR description.\n- **FIN-212:** The advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212\", so I couldn't read it myself. The fix relies on the test and the existing docstring.\n\nI haven't merged anything. Merging into main needs a code-owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason":