g", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring stating ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).\n\nNote: this changes rounding behavior for exact half-cent amounts (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66 instead of 2.67).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. The test expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`, so it failed.\n- **Fix:** I made a one-line change on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` so `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the new head (`0a9452f727`). That run also passed.\n- **Behaviour change:** Amounts that land exactly on a half cent now round to the nearest even cent instead of always up (e.g. `2.665` \u2192 `2.66`, not `2.67`). I noted this in the PR description.\n- **FIN-212:** The advisory lookup tool returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212\", so I couldn't read it myself. The fix relies on the test and the existing docstring.\n\nI haven't merged anything. Merging into main needs a code-owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}